### Page 2 of 12 (scanned page: machine OCR, may contain errors)

```text
Cheyenne will compensate the difference between the employee's City base pay and military base
pay, provided the military base pay is lower than the City base pay.Base pay is defined as the
regular pay the employee would have received from the City had they not been called to active
military duty.
Section6.CONTINUATION OF EMPLOYMENT.
Any employee covered by this ordinance who continues his orher term of employment
during and beyond the term of this ordinance shall be entitled to advancement annually (subject to
the provisions of Section 5), as set forth in Exhibit B, upon recommendation of the employee's
supervisor, if the mayor and council approve funds to pay the increases.
Section7.HEALTH, MEDICAL, DENTAL AND LIFE INSURANCE.
The Citywill negotiate with or seek bids from qualified health insurance providers andwill
enter into a contract with a qualified carrier or carriers to provide employees with a medical
insurance plan, which is on file in the Human Resources Department, for fiscal year 2019-2020
2020-2021.Each uniformed City employee eligiblefor health insurance coverage shall contribute
ten percent (10%) of the monthly health insurance premium attributable to the level of coverage
selected by that employee. This payment will be a payroll deduction.
The City will maintain dental insurance on employees pursuant to the dental plan on file in
wishes tomaintain dental insurance under this plan for eligible dependents as defined in Appendix
B of the dental plan, he or she may do so by paying the premium for the additional person(s)
insured.
The City will pay premiums for term life insurance on all employees in accordance with
the term life insurance plan on file in the Human Resources Department and City Clerk's Office.
Section 8. TERM.
The terms and conditions of employment set forth in this ordinance shall applyfor fiscal
year 2019-2020 2020-2021 and shall be approved as part of the budget process. This ordinance
will terminate at the beginning of fiscal year 2020-2021 2021-2022.
Section9.REPEAL OF OTHER ORDINANCES.
All other ordinances establishing specific terms and conditions of employment are
repealed.
Section10.SEVER ABILITY.
If any clause, sentence, paragraph or part of this ordinance or application to any person or
circumstance shallfor anyreasonbe adjudged by a court of competent jurisdiction tobeinvalid
such judgment shall not affect, impair or invalidate the remainder of this agreement.
Section 11.This ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its passage and publication.
FIRST READING:
SECOND READING:
THIRD AND FINAL READING:
Marian J. Orr, Mayor
